        description="Discounters hold 46.6% of German food-retail revenue (EHI, 2024 data) and remain Europe's fastest-growing physical channel outside Germany: Lidl grew 6.1% to EUR 140bn in FY2025, Aldi Nord grew 7.4% group-wide to about EUR 31bn (5.1% in Germany), Lidl GB reached a record 8.4% UK share in April 2026, and IGD sees discount growing 4.8% a year to 2030. In Germany itself the gain plateaued in 2025 (Edeka, Rewe and Lidl grew 2.7-3.6%; Aldi Süd +1.2%). Aldi US is adding 180+ stores in 2026 towards 3,200 by 2028 and claims one in three US households. Variety discounters (Action, Tedi, Woolworth) took 23% more non-food spend in two years (GfK) and set the visible price floor for branded hair and detergent packs. The pool mechanism is trade-margin dilution and price-ladder compression, not delisting.",
