        description="Edeka and Rewe alone hold 46.8% of German grocery and the trade press calls the power relations between the big four 'cemented' (NIQ Trade Dimensions data, 2025); buying alliances are re-forming rather than fading (Concordis: Carrefour and Coopérative U negotiating with multinational suppliers from 2026; Eurelec with E.Leclerc, Rewe and Ahold Delhaize sourcing jointly since 2025, Ahold Delhaize citing 'price differences between European countries that cannot be objectively explained'); consolidation continues (Carrefour exits Italy and Romania, 165 Auchan supermarkets rebannered to Intermarché from October 2026, Aldi US converting Southeastern Grocers). The EU Single Market Strategy (May 2025) commits to tackle territorial supply constraints, the legal lever alliances need to buy cross-border; until a proposal is tabled it stays a watch item inside this line.",
