        analysis="Weight in the answer: Social commerce as a scaled beauty channel offsets 0.06 of the 7.3 points of gross headwind, the twelfth largest tailwind of the 18 and the second tailwind in the Customer force. It is a hair-only driver and reaches 28 percent of the pool; the Customer pass-through (7.0 percent) and an overlap correction of 18 percent, shared with K-03 (buyer power), K-13 (retail media) and K-12 (drugstores) on the European hair cells, hold a driver with a modest Shift value in the lower half of the tailwinds.\n\nWhere it lands: Hair colour Europe (0.01 points) and hair care Europe (0.01 points) carry 35 percent of the effect; Europe holds 49 percent of the total, North America 23 percent and Asia and High Growth together 28 percent, a comparatively high share outside the two large regions, where the channel's live-commerce formats are most advanced. It offsets 4 percent of the hair styling contraction, 3 percent of hair colour and 3 percent of hair care. Its counterpart is X-16 (challenger fragmentation) in the Competitive force: this driver carries the new occasions and impulse volume the channel creates, X-16 carries the share the channel's native brands take, and the net of the pair is what the channel does to HCB.\n\nWhen it lands: An s-curve to 2030: 72 percent of the terminal effect is in the numbers by 2028, 93 percent by 2029, the half-way point is 2028 and the effect is complete by 2031.\n\nWhat the band hinges on: Its own range runs from 0.04 to 0.08 points. The channel is scaled (TikTok Shop US GMV USD 15.1bn in 2025 and USD 11.8bn in H1 2026, beauty and personal care its largest category, ten European markets live since June 2026) and the width is HCB's share of it, which is the open point, together with the margin caveat of platform commission plus 10 to 20 percent affiliate fees. The observables are Circana's TikTok Shop beauty series, the European GMV estimates (about EUR 500m across four continental markets in the 90 days to 9 July 2026) and the share of GMV from live commerce, a minority format in the West at about 8 percent of US attributed GMV; a plateau in the beauty share would argue for the lower end of the range.\n\nFigures: model attribution on the estimated HCB gross-profit mix, reconciled to a 2035 portfolio median of -5.6 percent (3 x 50,000 iterations, seed 42). Read as exposure if nobody acts, not as a forecast.",
